the first public appearance by new york  democratic governor andrew cuomo  since the bombshell revelations of  sexual harassment allegations  from the state attorney general and that  report from the a.g  meanwhile democratic state lawmakers are  deserting cuomo by the dozens as  impeachment talk  intensifies and the first of his alleged  victims to come forward  is taking the governor to court  correspondent brian yennis has tonight's  story from new york  today new york governor andrew cuomo was  spotted lounging poolside next to a  woman typing on a laptop  at the governor's mansion in albany  there is no sign he's resigning despite  pressure from democrats  just get the hell out of the way i mean  in the end maybe he could  close off his career with one act of  dignity and decency and just step aside  but don't bet on that according to the  new york post cuomo was bunkered up  wednesday inside the governor's mansion  locked up with his closest advisors  strategizing his next move  perhaps a press conference different  from tuesday's taped response  to respond to the damning investigation  which found he sexually harassed 11  employees  one of cuomo's staunches allies and  friends new york's democratic party  chair jay jacobs says  he was honest with the governor i was  very direct with the governor as to  where  support was and that he didn't have  the support anywhere that he needed it i  was very clear about that  according to the latest fox news count  there is enough support  in the state assembly and senate to  impeach and convict cuomo  in a letter to cuomo's lawyers today the  new york state assembly's judiciary  committee chair wrote quote  the committee's investigation is nearing  completion and the assembly will soon  consider potential articles of  impeachment  against your client i want  accountability not just  for the victims of the sexual harassment  but i want accountability for the 15  000 victims that died in the nursing  homes  the deadline for cuomo's lawyers to  submit defense evidence  is next friday the 13th meanwhile cuomo  accuser lindsey boylan is filing the  first civil lawsuit against the governor  for retaliation  her attorney releasing a statement  saying in part it was a calculated  effort  by the governor and his team to send a  message to ms boylan  and every other survivor to be quiet or  face the consequences  tonight cuomo's office says they will  cooperate with the assembly's  impeachment investigation and that the  governor  appreciates the opportunity to present  his perspective  brett brian yenis in new york brian  thank you
 

